---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology & Editorial Policy"
  description="How StitchCalc calculates yarn, gauge, fabric, and quilt figures, and how we review sources."
  canonicalPath="/methodology/"
>
  <h1 class="page-title">Methodology & editorial policy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>E-E-A-T commitments</h2>
    <p>
      We show formulas on every tool page, cite authoritative standards (especially the Craft Yarn Council),
      keep “last updated” dates visible, and separate planning estimates from pattern-tested yardage.
    </p>
    <h2>Calculation principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Pure functions in TypeScript with unit tests for every formula module.</li>
      <li>Unit conversions use exact factors (1 in = 2.54 cm; 1 yd = 0.9144 m; 1 oz = 28.349523125 g).</li>
      <li>Yarn density factors are CYC-category averages for planning—not brand-specific put-ups.</li>
      <li>Quilt HST formulas use traditional finished + ⅞" and eight-at-a-time (2×finished + 1.75").</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Review process</h2>
    <p>
      Placeholder reviewer: {siteConfig.reviewer.name}. Before launch, the owner should replace placeholders with real bios on
      <a href="/authors/">authors</a> and verify charts against primary sources after any CYC update.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with sources. Material formula changes update page dates and sitemap lastmod.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
